<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert IV, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1447–1508</span> · Also known as Albert the Wise</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert IV, called the Wise, was Duke of Bavaria-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> from 1465. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-landshut-succession">War of the Landshut Succession</a> of 1503–1505 he reunited the divided Wittelsbach duchies into a single Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, and in 1506 he decreed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primogeniture">primogeniture</a> so that the land would not be partitioned again. Munich became the permanent capital, and the Frauenkirche was completed early in his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-iv-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Albert IV, Duke of Bavaria" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Barthel Beham · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albert_IV,_Duke_of_Bavaria,_portrait_by_Barthel_Beham.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
